A home camera box follows one activity around the house today and needs a short Hebrew name for it, for messages to the homeowner like "<name> יצאו".

What the cameras saw of this activity (time, camera, people in view, what happened):
{{notes}}

Cameras: {{cameras}}. Most people seen at once: {{people}}.

Answer JSON only: {"name": "...", "plural": true or false}.

"name" is 1 to 4 words. It says WHO they are by their role or what they do, the way a homeowner would say it: "העובדים", "העובדים בפרגולה", "השליח", "הגנן", "בני הבית", "אורח בכניסה". Someone carrying tools, a ladder, a hose, cables or building materials, or working on the house, is a worker ("העובד" / "העובדים"); a group of workers is "העובדים". A place may be added only as a camera's name ("בפרגולה"). Never position or posture words ("ליד הקיר", "ליד הרכב", "עומד", "הולך"), never clothes or looks ("עם כובע", "בבגדים כהים"), never a camera id. When nothing says who it is, "אדם ב<the camera's name>" (or "אנשים ב..." for more than one).
"plural" is true when the name is about more than one person (a crew is plural even when one is in view).
